Edge: OpenResty/nginx ingress + optional XDP L4 filter. Compliance map policy: `compliance.mdc`. Parser alignment: `parser.mdc`, `hot-path.mdc`.

## Listeners

- :8180 HTTP/1.1
- :443 H2/H3/H1.1 ALPN
- Dev certs: `deploy/nginx/certs/generate-dev-certs.sh`
- Perimeter timeouts: `client_body_timeout` / `client_header_timeout` **5s**

## L7 pipeline (`access-check.lua`)

Rate limit -> circuit breaker -> blacklist cache -> body DFA (`edge-parse-dfa.lua`) -> per-campaign RL -> proxy to tracker pool (:8181-8184).

## Tracker ingress schema (`TRACKER_INGRESS_SCHEMA`)

Must match tracker config:

| Mode | Edge behavior | Tracker parse |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `openrtb_3` (default) | Read `request.item[0].id` | OpenRTB path |
| native track | Scan `campaign_id` in body | `ParseTrackRequestJSON*` / vtproto |

## POST /track edge-tracker parity (mandatory)

| Rule | Edge (`edge-phase2.lua`) | Tracker (`http1TrackEdgePolicy`) |
| :--- | :---: | :---: |
| `Content-Length` required | yes | yes |
| Chunked rejected | yes | yes |
| Duplicate/obfuscated `TE` rejected | yes | yes |

Chunked allowed on `POST /openrtb/bid` only.

Verify: `go test ./internal/ingestion/ -run=TestChaos_CrossHop_NginxGnet` — `differential_count=0`.

Implementation pairs: `http1TrackEdgePolicy` <-> `deploy/nginx/lua/edge-phase2.lua`; `http1IngressCanonical` for differential tests.

## Shard selection (must match Go)

```
slot  = crc32(campaign_id) & 1023
shard = slot_table[slot]
```

`edge-slot-map.lua` uses same Castagnoli CRC32C table as `sharding_amd64.s` / Go fallback. Control pushes slot table via outbox -> Redis shard 0 -> edge reload.

## GET /click

- Query-only; strict UUID `campaign_id`.
- Gate: `EDGE_EXPOSE_CLICK` (404 when off on edge).
- Tracker serves redirect on :8181-8184 regardless of edge flags.

## XDP (optional enterprise)

- Deny maps: control outbox -> Redis shard 0 -> `cmd/edge-bpf-sync` -> `/sys/fs/bpf/`.
- Attach: `cmd/edge-xdp`. Control never writes kernel maps directly.
- Decision path < 10 us; silent drop at NIC (no HTTP body for blocked IPs).
- Requires BTF, modern kernel. Not a substitute for L7 parser budgets.

## Tarpit

`EDGE_TARPIT_ENABLED=true` on nginx edge only; capped duration; never on billing/settlement paths.

## XDP (Enterprise)

Not appliance SKU. License `features.ebpf_xdp_edge`. Hot path must not import `internal/edge`.

Flow: control outbox → Redis shard 0 → `edge-bpf-sync` → BPF maps → `edge-xdp` drop → Nginx → tracker.

Pin dir default `/sys/fs/bpf/ad-event-processor`. Blocklist: host keys in LRU HASH (`/32`, `/128`); CIDR in LPM TRIE. Lookup: host HASH before prefix LPM. Allowlist before deny.

Scale: LPM `max_entries=786432`. Incremental sync via `blacklist:changelog:{add,remove}` ZSETs on shard 0; full `SMEMBERS` at startup + every 5 min.

| Binary | Role |
| :--- | :--- |
| `edge-xdp` | CAP_BPF + CAP_NET_ADMIN attach |
| `edge-bpf-sync` | Redis → maps; `SYNC_INTERVAL=5s` default |

OS fingerprint: edge forwards `X-TCP-TTL`, `X-TCP-WINDOW`, `X-TCP-MSS` from `edge-tcp-fp-sync` / XDP fingerprints map. CDN/L4 LB: set `OS_FINGERPRINT_MISMATCH_ENABLED=false` or accept skip metrics.

Rollback: stop bpf-sync → stop edge-xdp; Nginx Lua blacklist remains.

```bash
bash scripts/ci/compliance.sh
go test ./internal/edge/... -count=1
```

